en an eager agent  willing to prove himself is put into the  field too early he's got something to  prove he wants it too badly I understand  you feel responsible for him don't  patronize  dan feels responsible not only for the  deaths of his former agents but for the  families they leave behind this is why  he feels obligated to help Ellie's wife  and children by buying them supplies  cooking them breakfast and checking up  on them from time to time Nadya Cohen  Ellie's wife is in fact a real person  they married in 1959 and as the series  portrays she did not know about her  husband's involvement in Israeli  intelligence in the last episode we see  Ellie writing his final letter to her in  which he says the following I am begging  you my dear Nadia not to spend your time  and weeping about something already past  concentrate on yourself looking forward  for a better future remarry so that the  kids have a father and you have a  partner Nadia  never remarried she also had a third  child with Ellie a boy who is never  depicted in the show  Nadia would spend the rest of her life  commemorating Ellie and along with  Ellie's brother Maurice tried to get his  remains sent back to Israel Maurice  Cohen is another real character and as  depicted in the show attended to the  incoming telegrams for the Mossad and  like in the show discovered his  brother's secret identity while  decrypting incoming messages from agent  88 Ellie's codename Ellie Cohen was a  risky choice for the Israelis born in  Alexandria Egypt Ellie had a criminal  record for alleged scientist activities  following a military coup in 1951 when  the Egyptian government stepped up  Jewish persecution he moved to Israel in  1956 where he became a  counterintelligence analyst it was when  he was rejected by Mossad that he  resigned from the military and worked as  a filing clerk although Ellie was a  risky choice he was also perfect because  of his Arab background not only did he  speak Arabic he looked Arab 